    <string name="wk_guide_title">How to log an exercise</string>
    <string name="wk_guide_set">A set is one round of the exercise. Rest, then do the next set.</string>
    <string name="wk_guide_reps">Reps are how many times you did the movement in that set.</string>
    <string name="wk_guide_weight">Weight is the load you used. Leave it empty for bodyweight. First time? Pick a weight you can lift 12–15 times with good form.</string>
    <string name="wk_guide_effort">Effort: tap Easy, Good or Hard. If it was Easy two sessions in a row, add a little weight next time.</string>
    <string name="wk_guide_rest">The hourglass starts your rest after a set. Duration (stopwatch) times the whole exercise, mainly for cardio.</string>
    <string name="wk_guide_dismiss">Got it</string>
    <string name="wk_empty_hint_simple">Tap + to add an exercise, or ask Coach for a beginner routine for today.</string>
    <string name="settings_simple_logging">Simple view (beginners)</string>
    <string name="settings_simple_logging_footer">Sets ask Easy, Good or Hard instead of an RPE number, and show a short guide. Turn off for the expert view, where you type RPE.</string>
    <string name="wk_ask_coach_routine">Ask Coach for a routine</string>
    <string name="wk_coach_beginner_prompt">I am new to the gym. Build me a simple routine for today based on my profile and recent training: start with a short dynamic warm-up, then 4–6 easy-to-learn exercises (machines or bodyweight are fine) with sets and reps, and finish with a cool-down. Explain each exercise in one line and propose them for the workout of today.</string>
